---RadioGroup components are used to display a collection of options as a series of toggleable buttons.
---
---They support an arbitrary minimum and maximum number of selected options, allowing for both the usual radio control's
---single selection behaviour, and for a more flexible selection limit, with selection changes triggering
---`ONSELECTIONCHANGED` events hooks.
---
---They're ideal for situations where you have a set of mutually exclusive options, or want to allow users to mix and
---match multiple options (eg. category filters).
---
---Custom Visuals: Radio groups can make use of the same sprites as check components since they're essentially identical
---in terms of functionality.
---
---See here for information on how to create custom sprites that are usable by radio groups.
---@class ui.RadioGroup : ui.Component
---@field numSelected integer (Read-only) The number of currently selected options.
---@field selectedValues integer[] (Read-only) Array containing the IDs or values of the currently selected entries.
---@field selectedLabels string[] (Read-only) Array containing the text labels of the currently selected entries.
---@field entryMargin ui.Margin (Modifiable Contents) Offsets used to determine the inner content area within the regions for the individual options.
---@field labelsText ui.TextData (Modifiable Contents) Text properties used when displaying option text labels.
---@field buttonSprite ui.SpriteData (Modifiable Contents) Sprite properties used for the radiogroup's buttons.
ui.RadioGroup = {}

---Creates a new radiogroup on the specified parent.
---
---Warning: Creating a component can fail if there's already a component on that parent with the same category ID and
---dynamic ID, or if those are omitted and the application is unable to generate a valid ID for the component.
---@param parent ui.ComponentCollection Parent component to create this radiogroup in.
---@param categoryID? integer Category ID used to identify this component. Defaults to the parent's category ID if not specified.
---@param dynamicID? integer Dynamic ID used to identify this component. Defaults to auto-incrementing from the parent's dynamic ID if not specified.
---@return ui.RadioGroup # The newly created radiogroup. The caller must set its layout and visual information afterwards.
function ui.RadioGroup.new(parent, categoryID, dynamicID) end

---Adds an option to the radiogroup.
---@param id integer Unique value identifying this option.
---@param label string Text to display for this option.
---@return boolean # True if successful, false if an option with that ID already exists.
function ui.RadioGroup:Add(id, label) end

---Removes the option associated with this ID.
---@param id integer Value used to identify the option to remove.
---@return boolean # Indicates whether or not an option was successfully removed.
function ui.RadioGroup:Remove(id) end

---Returns whether or not there's an option associated with the provided ID.
---@param id integer Value associated with the option to check.
---@return boolean # True if there is an option corresponding to the provided ID, false otherwise.
function ui.RadioGroup:HasOption(id) end

---Clears existing options from the radiogroup and adds all options in the provided container to the radiogroup.
---
---Warning: Entry IDs are expected to be unique, if the provided ID is already used by another option, this function
---will fail and return false.
---@param entries table<string, integer> Table containing a mapping between option names and their IDs to add to the radiogroup.
---@return boolean # True if the provided options were valid and were successfully added to the radiogroup, false otherwise. This function can fail and return false due to the provided ID already existing, or due to invalid/malformed data.
function ui.RadioGroup:SetOptions(entries) end

---Gets the value/ID associated with the `selectionIndex` selected entry.
---@param selectionIndex integer Index into the currently selected entries collection to access.
---@return integer # The value/ID associated with the entry, or -1 if there are less than `selectionIndex` selected entries.
function ui.RadioGroup:GetSelectedValue(selectionIndex) end

---Gets the text label associated with the `selectionIndex` selected entry.
---@param selectionIndex integer Index into the currently selected entries collection to access.
---@return string # The text label associated with the entry, or an empty string if there are less than `selectionIndex` selected entries.
function ui.RadioGroup:GetSelectedLabel(selectionIndex) end

---Gets whether the option associated with the specified ID is enabled and can be selected by the user.
---@param id integer Value associated with the desired option.
---@return boolean # True if the desired option exists and is enabled, false otherwise.
function ui.RadioGroup:GetOptionEnabled(id) end

---Sets whether the option associated with the specified ID is enabled and can be selected by the user.
---@param id integer Value associated with the desired option.
---@param enabled boolean Whether or not the option should be enabled and selectable by the user.
---@return boolean # True if the desired option exists, false otherwise.
function ui.RadioGroup:SetOptionEnabled(id, enabled) end

---Gets whether the option associated with the specified ID is currently selected.
---@param id integer Value associated with the desired option.
---@return boolean # True if the desired option exists and is selected, false otherwise.
function ui.RadioGroup:GetOptionSelected(id) end

---Sets whether the option associated with the specified ID is currently selected, optionally triggering selection
---events.
---
---Info: This method obeys selection limits and will not make any changes if this would have resulted in the radiogroup
---being in an invalid state.
---@param id integer Value associated with the desired option.
---@param selected boolean Whether or not the option should be selected currently. Defaults to false.
---@param triggerEvents? boolean
---@return boolean # True if the desired option exists, false otherwise.
function ui.RadioGroup:SetOptionSelected(id, selected, triggerEvents) end

---Sets the parameters used to position and layout the various options within this radiogroup.
---@param numColumns integer Number of columns to split the various radiogroup contents over.
---@param spacing integer Desired horizontal and vertical spacing between each option.
---@param buttonSize integer Controls whether to display options as toggle buttons or as checks. If set to `0`, options are displayed as toggle buttons, otherwise this controls the size of the checkbox for each option.
---@param buttonLabelSpacing integer
function ui.RadioGroup:SetVisualParams(numColumns, spacing, buttonSize, buttonLabelSpacing) end

---Changes the minimum and maximum number of selected options, without changing how many options are currently selected.
---@param minSelectedEntries integer Minimum number of entries that can be selected at any one time.
---@param maxSelectedEntries integer Maximum number of entries that can be selected at any one time.
---@return boolean # True if the `minSelectedEntries` and `maxSelectedEntries` form a valid range, where the minimum is less than or equal to maximum, and were set successfully, false otherwise.
function ui.RadioGroup:SetSelectionLimits(minSelectedEntries, maxSelectedEntries) end
